module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.refusal_producer_lands_without_its_ownership_row

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data refusal_producer_lands_without_its_ownership_row: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refusal_producer_lands_without_its_ownership_row" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a front-end stage gains a producer of a fatal refusal reason (a new `^..._reason_...` symbol, or an old one newly reachable) while `v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership` `known_frontier_causes` carries no row for it. The producer and its ownership are two facts in two files, and the only join between them is `gunbc.witness_v2_native_route` `native_route_exclusions_all_classified` / `native_route_file_refusals_attributed`, executed by the native route, which is off the merge path (gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path).",
    "HARM: the native route refuses its OWN admission by name (`unattributed_exclusions_present`, `unattributed_file_refusals_present`), so `//gunbc/instruments:v2-native-frontier` prints NOT A MEASUREMENT and can say neither green nor red about the native route. Every other clause may hold and it still does not measure; the one run that would say so is the run nobody on the landing path executes.",
    "OBSERVED on main 1457bd81d00 (swift-ant-539, BuildBuddy, `claim_executor --v2-native-route`, driver-rows.jsonl aggregated in the same dispatch): positive population, required native pass and both live controls HELD; admission refused only on the two unattributed clauses. The unowned fatal causes were `body_lowering_reason_unsupported_form` (producers added by gunbc#12245 and gunbc#12315), `body_lowering_reason_function_value_body_unread` (gunbc#12210) and `infer_match_shape_invalid` (an older infer producer that became reachable as more modules cleared body lowering). None had ever had a row. The same two refusals held at the head of gunbc#12420 (4475ef4dd29).",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: not a frontier REGRESSION -- the refused members were already refused under some cause, and the new cause only renamed where they stop; not a missing measurement of the positive population -- that clause and the live pair were observed. The earlier refusals reported against eb5987e38f5 / cfc470cf (positive_population_empty, required_native_pass_regressed, both controls unobserved) do NOT reproduce on 1457bd81d00; at 19f039b6462 (parent of gunbc#12392) the smoke member reached EVAL and refused `eval_rejected_invalid_node`, so that was a separate eval defect since fixed on main, not the caret refusal's import cascade.",
    "RECURRED on main 55e78f40e9a, the day after gunbc#12626 owned the first three: `//gunbc/instruments:v2-native-frontier` refused admission on `unattributed_exclusions_present` alone, with six PREPARE exclusions all fatal on `infer_match_scrutinee_not_bool` (v2.compiler.04_infer, producer present since gunbc#10485), all in v2.test.claim.determinism_contract_test. The producer was old and newly reachable, as with `infer_match_shape_invalid`: the recurrence is the class's ceiling argument, since every module that clears an earlier stage can surface a producer nobody rostered, and the merge-path join named below is what would have refused it on the landing that made it reachable.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigated -- the admission refuses loudly and by name, so nothing passes silently, but the refusal fires after the fact on a run no merge waits for. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the set of refusal reasons a stage can produce is derivable from the stage's own source, so an unowned producible reason can be refused before merge. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the native route's admission executes on the landing path (the frontier in the required lane, gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path's trigger), so a PR that adds an unowned producer is refused by these same clauses before it merges; or, sufficient on its own, a merge-path claim that joins every fatal-reason symbol a front-end stage can emit to an ownership row at identity grain.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
